1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,051
The gate decision converts evidence into action.

2
00:00:03,121 --> 00:00:08,795
Land when the critical assumption holds and
remaining operational conditions are satisfied.

3
00:00:08,865 --> 00:00:13,964
Iterate when the mechanism remains plausible
but a bounded defect needs correction.

4
00:00:14,034 --> 00:00:17,938
Pivot when evidence points toward a
different problem or intervention.

5
00:00:18,008 --> 00:00:22,424
Stop when the approach lacks value
or exceeds an unacceptable boundary.

6
00:00:22,494 --> 00:00:28,126
Explain the choice using evidence, risk,
reversibility, and the next observable test.

7
00:00:28,196 --> 00:00:33,871
Three variants appear: speed improves but
errors double; category assistance has no effect

8
00:00:33,941 --> 00:00:38,911
because account lookup dominates; and
a prototype sends unauthorized replies.

9
00:00:38,981 --> 00:00:41,328
Each failure demands a different decision.

10
00:00:41,398 --> 00:00:46,177
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

11
00:00:46,247 --> 00:00:50,321
Assign a gate decision to each
variant and state the next action.

12
00:00:50,391 --> 00:00:55,447
Iterate on excessive routing errors if a
specific correction can be tested safely.

13
00:00:55,517 --> 00:00:59,848
Pivot toward account lookup when
evidence changes the problem mechanism.

14
00:00:59,918 --> 00:01:05,230
Stop unauthorized replies and restore the
approval boundary before further testing.

15
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:10,847
A stop can be temporary for recovery, but
continuing unchanged would ignore the evidence.

16
00:01:10,917 --> 00:01:14,095
What is the correct response
to an unauthorized action?

17
00:01:14,165 --> 00:01:17,643
A. Stop the action path
and recover the boundary B.

18
00:01:17,713 --> 00:01:19,633
Ignore it if speed improved C.

19
00:01:19,703 --> 00:01:21,025
Change the metric.

20
00:01:21,095 --> 00:01:22,546
The best answer is A.

21
00:01:22,616 --> 00:01:26,136
A favorable average does not
cancel an authority breach.
